{"name":"A Lot of Love","hex":"#ffbcc5","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Lotuko."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large quantity or number; a great deal.","A separate, appropriated portion; a quantized, subdivided set consisting a whole."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lot"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Lot of Love","blocks":[{"text":"A Lot of Love is the fifteenth album by American singer Melba Moore. It was released by Capitol Records on July 18, 1986. This album featured two number-one R&B hits, including the duet, \"A Little Bit More\", with Freddie Jackson and \"Falling\". She scored other popular R&B hits including \"Love the One I'm With \" and \"It's Been So Long\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/A_Lot_of_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Lot_of_Love","wikidata":"Q4657954"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d7/A_Lot_of_Love.jpg/250px-A_Lot_of_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par